WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.640
 Instead of naming a specific model like this Llama 3.1, I want to use the Dynamic Routes feature

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.480
 in Cloudflare's AI Gateway.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:12.920
 So I'm changing this to use the dynamic/support route, and I'm doing a small change of going

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:17.140
 to the compat endpoint versus the Workers AI v1 endpoint.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:19.960
 That is so that we can support for this dynamic route.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:25.720
 So again, just a simple URL change, and now we're changing the model that we want to use.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.880
 And in this case, it's a dynamic model.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.960
 So looking back in our AI gateway, we can look at our dynamic models.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.760
 I have this one called support, which is the one that we've just chosen to use.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:42.280
 And what it does is it actually makes choices based on the metadata and those choices determine

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:44.380
 which model is going to be called.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.160
 So the rule here is pretty simple.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:51.720
 If you're on the intern team, you get a more economical model, in this case Llama 3.1.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:58.160
 Everyone else, so our escalation engineers, get a more capable model like Llama 3.3 with

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.840
 a model fallback as well.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:06.360
 So if that 3.3 for whatever reason is failing, we can fall back to this OpenAI GPT-OSS model.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:11.320
 And what this really unlocks is that now your route lives inside of your gateway.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:12.480
 We can change the routes.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:13.760
 We can modify the routes.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:19.880
 If a new model comes out, we can change this choice here to a different model without having

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:24.960
 to redeploy our application or application already is pointing at this dynamic support

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:25.960
 route.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:29.360
 We can change the models within that route without making deployments.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:34.000
 And that's really great and really unlocks a lot of capabilities for us.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.240
 Maybe we want to start trying something out for the interns.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:39.760
 We can easily change the model they're using without having to make a deployment.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:43.360
 This is instantly making the changes out to your AI gateway.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.200
 So let's see this in action.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.040
 I can go back to this.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.200
 This version is now using the dynamic route.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:54.160
 I can go use our support case here with Riley.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:55.720
 Send this through.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:01.360
 And we can see that this Llama 3.1 was chosen by our route, which is perfect.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:03.960
 This is going through our dynamic route.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:09.400
 I'll refresh and I will now go with Sam, who is an escalation engineer.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.120
 He is no longer an intern.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:16.720
 I will send this request and we can see that we're using that dynamic/support route and now

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.960
 getting Llama 3.3.

